  "text": "Five hundred salespeople. Every month, each one's number is their skill, plus luck. Take the top tenth in month one. They averaged a hundred and thirty-two. The same people, the next month... a hundred and thirteen. The bottom tenth went the other way, from seventy up to ninety-five. Nobody did anything. Part of every extreme score was luck, and luck doesn't repeat. Coach that bottom group, and they'd improve anyway... and the coaching would get the credit. To credit it, you'd need a control group, just as extreme, and left alone. The next traps come from choosing what you look at.",
